[TITLE]
Pattern attachment fixture -- ROADMAP Task 248.02. A reservoir on a HEAD pattern and a
pump on a SPEED pattern, the two attachment points EPA's own Net1/Net2/Net3 never use.
Hand-written, and deliberately TWO components so each anchor is exact: the flow through
P1 and through PU1 is the junction demand and nothing else, so a head that moves can only
have moved because the pattern moved it.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID     Elev    Demand  Pattern
 J1     50      200
 J2     50      150

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID     Head    Pattern
 R1     200.0   RHEAD
 R2     10

[PIPES]
;ID     Node1   Node2   Length  Diam    Rough   MinorLoss  Status
 P1     R1      J1      1000    12      130     0          Open

[PUMPS]
;ID     Node1   Node2   Parameters
 PU1    R2      J2      HEAD C1  SPEED 1.20  PATTERN PSPD

[CURVES]
;ID     Flow    Head
 C1     0       150
 C1     200     120
 C1     400     60

[PATTERNS]
;ID     Multipliers
 RHEAD  1.05  0.98  0.96  0.94  0.92  0.90
 RHEAD  0.92  0.94  0.96  0.98  1.0   1.02
 PSPD   1.15  1.05  1.10  0.95  0.90  1.0
 PSPD   1.0   1.05  1.10  0.95  0.90  1.0

[TIMES]
 Duration             11:00
 Hydraulic Timestep   1:00
 Pattern Timestep     1:00
 Report Timestep      1:00

[OPTIONS]
 Units                GPM
 Headloss             H-W
 Accuracy             1e-8
 Trials               200
 Unbalanced           Continue 10

[COORDINATES]
;Node   X-Coord   Y-Coord
 R1     0         100
 J1     300       100
 R2     0         300
 J2     300       300

[END]
